"geo\":{\"bgcolor\":\"white\",\"landcolor\":\"#E5ECF6\",\"subunitcolor\":\"white\",\"showland\":true,\"showlakes\":true,\"lakecolor\":\"white\"},\"title\":{\"x\":0.05},\"mapbox\":{\"style\":\"light\"},\"margin\":{\"b\":0,\"l\":0,\"r\":0,\"t\":30}}},\"geo\":{\"projection\":{\"type\":\"natural earth\"},\"lataxis\":{\"range\":[-10,60]},\"lonaxis\":{\"range\":[-100,145]},\"showcountries\":true,\"countrycolor\":\"#bbb\",\"showcoastlines\":true,\"coastlinecolor\":\"#999\",\"showland\":true,\"landcolor\":\"#f7f7f7\",\"showocean\":true,\"oceancolor\":\"#e8eef2\"},\"margin\":{\"l\":0,\"r\":0,\"t\":10,\"b\":10},\"font\":{\"family\":\"Inter, sans-serif\",\"color\":\"#1a1a1a\"},\"legend\":{\"orientation\":\"h\",\"yanchor\":\"bottom\",\"y\":-0.05,\"x\":0,\"bgcolor\":\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\"},\"height\":520,\"paper_bgcolor\":\"rgba(0,0,0,0)\"},                        {\"responsive\": true}                    ).then(function(){\n                            \nvar gd = document.getElementById('d675dcfd-d0b5-4967-839c-309136c51ede');\nvar x = new MutationObserver(function (mutations, observer) {{\n        var display = window.getComputedStyle(gd).display;\n        if (!display || display === 'none') {{\n            console.log([gd, 'removed!']);\n            Plotly.purge(gd);\n            observer.disconnect();\n        }}\n}});\n\n// Listen for the removal of the full notebook cells\nvar notebookContainer = gd.closest('#notebook-container');\nif (notebookContainer) {{\n    x.observe(notebookContainer, {childList: true});\n}}\n\n// Listen for the clearing of the current output cell\nvar outputEl = gd.closest('.output');\nif (outputEl) {{\n    x.observe(outputEl, {childList: true});\n}}\n\n                        })                };            </script>        </div>\n```\n\nSummer 2026 itinerary across six destinations and three regions. East Asia leg covers Hong Kong, southern mainland China and Seoul; Southeast Asia leg covers Vietnam (Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh City); Americas leg covers Miami and New York. Hover any marker to see what I am most looking forward to in each.\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## What I want to bring back\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"fg-bring-back\">\n\n  <div class=\"fg-bring-back__item\">\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__icon\"><i class=\"bi bi-globe2\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__title\">Direct experience of Asian markets</div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__body\">Reading about Asian consumer behaviour and seeing it on the ground are two different things. Density, payment behaviour (mobile-first to a degree Western markets are not), retail formats, the way digital and physical interact. Useful for any analytics role where the dataset is global.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fg-bring-back__item\">\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__icon\"><i class=\"bi bi-translate\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__title\">Spanish practice in Miami</div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__body\">Miami is one of the few US cities where Spanish is more useful than English in many neighbourhoods. A few weeks of forced immersion is a more efficient way to push my Spanish from intermediate toward upper-intermediate than another six months of textbook study.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fg-bring-back__item\">\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__icon\"><i class=\"bi bi-people-fill\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__title\">A network across three continents</div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__body\">Travel is the most efficient mechanism for building relationships outside your existing network. Even a small set of contacts in each region is a structural advantage in a career where remote and cross-region work is increasingly the norm.</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"fg-bring-back__item\">\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__icon\"><i class=\"bi bi-arrow-clockwise\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__title\">Reset before the next chapter</div>\n    <div class=\"fg-bring-back__body\">Three months between finishing one demanding thing (a final-year degree) and starting another (a graduate analyst role) is unusually rare. Using it deliberately, rather than letting it drift, is the specific point.</div>\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n```\n\n",
